          Use automated tools like XCA (X Certificate and Key Management) to batch create certificates
          Create certificates with specific extensions to enable specific attack scenarios (e.g., code signing)
          Generate certificates using weak cryptographic parameters to enable future attacks
          Create certificates that mimic legitimate CA-issued certificates in appearance
