          Use PowerShell New-SelfSignedCertificate cmdlet for certificate generation
          Generate certificates through Java's keytool utility
          Create certificates with specific extended key usage for code signing
          Generate wildcard certificates to sign multiple applications
          Create certificates with long validity periods to avoid frequent renewals
          Use cross-signed certificates to establish chain of trust
          Use XCA (X Certificate and Key Management) GUI tool for certificate creation
          Implement automated certificate generation through scripting frameworks
          Create certificates mimicking legitimate trusted publishers' information
          Generate certificates using specific cryptographic algorithms (e.g., RSA-4096, ECC)
          Use DigiCert Certificate Utility for certificate generation and management
