          Implement rule using delegated mailbox access to maintain persistence across accounts
          Configure rule to leverage Outlook add-in extensibility for code execution
          Create rule that persists through Cached Exchange Mode synchronization
          Set up rule using Graph API to maintain persistence in Microsoft 365
          Implement rule that triggers on message recall attempts
          Create rule combining client and server-side actions for redundant persistence
          Configure rule to execute based on digital signature verification status
          Set up rule that leverages Outlook's Smart Alert system
          Create rule that persists through AutoArchive operations
          Create rule leveraging Outlook's offline mode for disconnected persistence
          Implement rule that persists through Exchange Server role changes
          Configure rule to execute based on Distribution List membership changes
          Create rule that triggers on message classification changes
          Set up rule using OAuth token manipulation for persistent access
          Implement rule that survives Outlook profile repair operations
          Create rule targeting shared mailbox synchronization events
          Configure rule to persist through Exchange hybrid deployment transitions
          Set up rule leveraging retention policy triggers
          Create rule that maintains persistence during mailbox journaling
        Add-ins: Adversaries may abuse Microsoft Office add-ins to obtain persistence on a compromised system. Office add-ins can be used to add functionality to Office programs. (Citation: Microsoft Office Add-ins) There are different types of add-ins that can be used by the various Office products; including Word/Excel add-in Libraries (WLL/XLL), VBA add-ins, Office Component Object Model (COM) add-ins, automation add-ins, VBA Editor (VBE), Visual Studio Tools for Office (VSTO) add-ins, and Outlook add-ins. (Citation: MRWLabs Office Persistence Add-ins)(Citation: FireEye Mail CDS 2018)  Add-ins can be used to obtain persistence because they can be set to execute code when an Office application starts.
          Create malicious Excel XLL add-in and place in Excel's add-in directory to execute at startup
          Deploy COM add-in via registry key HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\Microsoft\Office\[Office Version]\[Office Application]\Addins
          Create malicious Outlook Form Region add-in to execute code when Outlook starts
          Install VSTO add-in through ClickOnce deployment manifest to maintain persistence
          Modify VBA add-in settings in Normal.dotm template to load malicious macro at Word startup
