          Exploit vulnerable network equipment to modify traffic at routing/switching level
          Install compromised network protocol libraries to modify data during serialization/deserialization
          Modify database replication traffic by intercepting and altering binary log streams
          Insert malicious proxy configurations into application settings to route traffic through attacker infrastructure
          Use DLL hijacking to intercept and modify inter-process communication (IPC) messages
          Deploy compromised file transfer protocols (FTP/SFTP) clients that modify data during transfer
          Implement memory hooks to intercept and modify data in shared memory segments
          Exploit cloud service API gateways to modify data in transit between microservices
          Use malicious browser extensions to modify web application data before submission
          Modify backup data streams during transmission to backup storage
          Intercept and modify EDI (Electronic Data Interchange) transactions between business systems
          Deploy compromised message queue clients that modify data before publication
        Runtime Data Manipulation: Adversaries may modify systems in order to manipulate the data as it is accessed and displayed to an end user, thus threatening the integrity of the data.(Citation: FireEye APT38 Oct 2018)(Citation: DOJ Lazarus Sony 2018) By manipulating runtime data, adversaries may attempt to affect a business process, organizational understanding, and decision making.  Adversaries may alter application binaries used to display data in order to cause runtime manipulations. Adversaries may also conduct [Change Default File Association](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1546/001) and [Masquerading](https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1036) to cause a similar effect. The type of modification and the impact it will have depends on the target application and process as well as the goals and objectives of the adversary. For complex systems, an adversary would likely need special expertise and possibly access to specialized software related to the system that would typically be gained through a prolonged information gathering campaign in order to have the desired impact.
          Patch application binary to modify data display functions using hex editors or binary patching tools
          Use API hooking tools like Microsoft Detours to intercept and modify data processing functions
          Inject malicious DLLs into running processes to alter data handling routines
          Modify process memory using tools like Process Hacker to change runtime values
          Implement userland hooks to intercept and modify system calls related to data processing
          Use memory scanning tools to locate and modify specific data patterns in running applications
