          Insert timing-based triggers into model architecture that activate under specific deployment conditions
          Modify model compression layers to selectively preserve malicious behaviors while appearing optimized
          Insert architecture components that exploit specific numeric precision limitations
          Modify model architecture to create resource exhaustion in model serving systems
          Insert cross-model dependency chains that enable coordinated attacks across deployed models
          Modify architecture to bypass model validation checks in deployment pipelines
          Insert specialized layers that exploit specific framework version vulnerabilities
          Modify model architecture during framework conversion to insert undetectable malicious operations
          Insert architecture modifications that exploit specific edge device limitations
          Modify mixture-of-experts routing to selectively activate malicious expert networks
          Insert architecture changes that survive model pruning and quantization while maintaining malicious behavior
          Modify transformer attention patterns to create selective blind spots in model processing
          Insert architecture modifications that exploit specific mobile device constraints
          Modify model architecture to create vulnerabilities during model merging or ensemble operations
          Insert specialized layers that exploit AutoML/Neural Architecture Search systems
          Modify architecture to create silent failures during model optimization steps
          Insert cross-platform incompatibilities that trigger specific behaviors in different environments
        Embed Malware: Adversaries may embed malicious code into AI Model files. AI models may be packaged as a combination of instructions and weights. Some formats such as pickle files are unsafe to deserialize because they can contain unsafe calls such as exec. Models with embedded malware may still operate as expected. It may allow them to achieve Execution, Command & Control, or Exfiltrate Data.
